### 6.2 Certificates Table
| Column | Data | Sortable |
|---|---|---|
| Certificate ID | `ISO27-2026-XXXXXXXX` (copy icon) | — |
| Holder Name | `full_name` from certificate | ✅ |
| Email | User email | — |
| Track | Associate / Professional badge | — |
| Score | Score at time of award | ✅ |
| Awarded On | Date + time | ✅ |
| Status | Active (green) / Revoked (red) | ✅ |
| Actions | [View] [Revoke] or [Reinstate] | — |

### 6.3 Certificate Detail Drawer
- Certificate preview thumbnail (loads from R2 URL).
- Full metadata: holder, email, track, score, session ID, awarded date, revocation status.
- **Verification link** — opens `/verify/:cert_id` in a new tab.
- **Download links** — landscape JPEG, square JPEG.
- **Revocation Section:**
  - If active: [Revoke Certificate] button opens a confirmation modal requiring a reason.
  - If revoked: shows revocation reason, date, revoking admin's email. [Reinstate] button available.

### 6.4 Revocation Flow
1. Admin clicks [Revoke Certificate].
2. Confirmation modal: "This action will set the certificate as invalid on the public verification page. Enter a reason:"
3. Admin enters reason → clicks [Confirm Revoke].
4. API: `PATCH /api/admin/certificates/:cert_id/revoke` → sets `revoked = true`, `revoked_reason = reason`.
5. The public `/verify/:cert_id` page now shows "REVOKED" status.
6. An email is sent to the certificate holder notifying them of the revocation.

