## 7. View 5 — Question Flags (`/admin/flags`)

### 7.1 Purpose
Users can flag a question during the Results screen ("Report inaccuracy" link under each question). This view allows admins to review all flagged questions, take action, and feed corrections back into the AI prompt tuning process.

### 7.2 Schema — question_flags table (new)
```sql
CREATE TABLE question_flags (
  id                UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  exam_session_id   UUID REFERENCES exam_sessions(id),
  user_id           UUID REFERENCES users(id),
  question_id       TEXT NOT NULL,            -- e.g. "A-T1-0012"
  question_stem     TEXT NOT NULL,            -- full question text at time of flagging
  flag_reason       TEXT NOT NULL,            -- user-provided freetext, max 500 chars
  status            TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'
                    CHECK (status IN ('open','reviewed','dismissed','escalated')),
  admin_note        TEXT,
  reviewed_by       UUID REFERENCES users(id),
  reviewed_at       TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at        TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_question_flags_question_id ON question_flags(question_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_question_flags_status ON question_flags(status);
```

### 7.3 Flags Table
| Column | Data | Sortable |
|---|---|---|
| Question ID | e.g. `A-T1-0012` | — |
| Flag Count | How many users flagged this exact question_id | ✅ |
| Domain | Derived from thread number | — |
| Track | Associate / Professional | — |
| Status | Open / Reviewed / Dismissed / Escalated badge | ✅ |
| Last Flagged | Most recent `created_at` | ✅ |
| Actions | [Review] | — |

- Default sort: unreviewed flags first, then by flag count descending.
- **Filters:** Status, Track, Domain/Thread.
- Questions are **grouped by `question_id`** — if 5 users flagged the same question, it appears as one row with flag count = 5.

### 7.4 Flag Detail Drawer
- **Question stem** (full text, large readable format).
- **All 4 answer options** with the correct option highlighted.
- **Explanation** as generated by AI.
- **Clause Reference** (e.g., "ISO 27001:2022 Clause 6.1.2").
- **Individual Flag Reports** — table of each flag submission: user email, their submitted reason, date.
- **Actions:**
  - **Mark as Reviewed + Add Admin Note** — status → `reviewed`, stores admin note.
  - **Dismiss** — status → `dismissed` (flag was inaccurate/user error).
  - **Escalate** — status → `escalated` (question has real error, needs prompt engineering fix).

### 7.5 Escalated Questions
- Escalated flags appear on a dedicated sub-tab within this view.
- Admin can add notes for future prompt tuning: "Thread 3 prompt needs stronger distractor guidance for Clause 8.2."
- Escalated questions can be added to a **blocklist** (`question_blocklist` table, keyed by `stem_hash`) so that exact question is excluded from future sessions.

### 7.6 Schema — question_blocklist table (new)
```sql
CREATE TABLE question_blocklist (
  id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  stem_hash       TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  question_id     TEXT,
  reason          TEXT,
  added_by        UUID REFERENCES users(id),
  created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

### 7.7 API — Question Flags
```
GET /api/admin/flags?page=1&limit=25&status=open&track=&thread=
  Response: { data: FlagGroup[], total, page, pages }
  -- FlagGroup: { question_id, question_stem, flag_count, track, thread, status, last_flagged }

GET /api/admin/flags/:question_id
  Response: { question, individual_flags: Flag[] }

PATCH /api/admin/flags/:question_id/review
  Body: { note: string }
  Response: { success: true }

PATCH /api/admin/flags/:question_id/dismiss
  Response: { success: true }

PATCH /api/admin/flags/:question_id/escalate
  Body: { note: string }
  Response: { success: true }

POST /api/admin/flags/:question_id/blocklist
  Body: { reason: string }
  Response: { success: true }
```

