## 8. View 6 — Buffer Pool (`/admin/buffer-pool`)

### 8.1 Purpose
The Buffer Pool is a set of pre-validated, human-reviewed questions used as fallback when AI generation fails for a thread. It must always contain ≥ 200 questions per track (100 per thread × 2 tracks). Admins manage this pool from this view.

### 8.2 Layout
- **Track tabs** at top: Associate | Professional
- Within each track: **Thread sub-tabs** (Thread 1–5, labeled with domain name)
- Each tab shows the question list for that track + thread combination.
- **Stats bar:** "137 / 200 questions (68%)" — shows how full the buffer is. Red if < 50%.

### 8.3 Buffer Questions Table
| Column | Data |
|---|---|
| Question ID | `A-T1-0001` format |
| Stem Preview | First 80 chars of question stem |
| Difficulty | Easy / Medium / Hard badge |
| Clause Ref | e.g., `6.1.2` |
| Times Used | How many times this was pulled as a fallback |
| Added On | Date admin added it |
| Actions | [View / Edit] [Delete] |

### 8.4 Add Question Flow
1. Admin clicks **[+ Add Question]** button (top right).
2. A modal/form opens with fields matching the Question Object JSON Schema (Section 4.2 of PRD-v2):
   - Question Stem (textarea)
   - Option A / B / C / D (4 text inputs)
   - Correct Option (radio: A / B / C / D)
   - Explanation (textarea)
   - Clause Reference (text)
   - Difficulty (select: Easy / Medium / Hard)
   - Thread (1–5, auto-set from active tab but editable)
3. On submit: frontend validates against the same AJV schema used in the backend.
4. POST to `/api/admin/buffer-pool` — backend re-validates schema, generates `question_id`, sets `is_buffer = true`, inserts into PostgreSQL.
5. Success: question appears in the table; modal closes.

### 8.5 Edit Question
- Same form as Add, pre-filled.
- PUT to `/api/admin/buffer-pool/:question_id`.

### 8.6 Import via JSON (Bulk Upload)
- **[Import JSON]** button opens a textarea.
- Admin pastes a JSON array of question objects.
- Frontend validates each object against the schema and shows a preview table with validation errors highlighted per row.
- Admin confirms → bulk POST to `/api/admin/buffer-pool/import`.
- Response: `{ imported: 45, skipped: 3, errors: [{ row: 12, error: "missing clause_ref" }] }`

### 8.7 API — Buffer Pool
```
GET /api/admin/buffer-pool?track=associate&thread=1
  Response: { data: BufferQuestion[], total, track_total }

POST /api/admin/buffer-pool
  Body: QuestionObject
  Response: { success: true, question_id: string }

PUT /api/admin/buffer-pool/:question_id
  Body: Partial<QuestionObject>
  Response: { success: true }

DELETE /api/admin/buffer-pool/:question_id
  Response: { success: true }

POST /api/admin/buffer-pool/import
  Body: { questions: QuestionObject[] }
  Response: { imported: number, skipped: number, errors: ImportError[] }

GET /api/admin/buffer-pool/stats
  Response: {
    associate: { total: number, by_thread: { [1..5]: number } },
    professional: { total: number, by_thread: { [1..5]: number } }
  }
```

