## 9. View 7 — Admin Audit Log (future, Phase 7)

All admin actions are logged in an `admin_audit_log` table for accountability. This view exposes the log in read-only format. Not required for Phase 6 MVP but the **backend logging must be implemented from Phase 6 onwards**.

### 9.1 Schema — admin_audit_log (log from Phase 6)
```sql
CREATE TABLE admin_audit_log (
  id           UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  admin_id     UUID REFERENCES users(id),
  action       TEXT NOT NULL,    -- e.g. "revoke_certificate", "block_user", "add_buffer_question"
  target_type  TEXT NOT NULL,    -- "certificate", "user", "session", "question"
  target_id    TEXT NOT NULL,    -- the id/uuid of the affected resource
  metadata     JSONB,            -- before/after state, reason, etc.
  ip_address   TEXT,
  created_at   TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

### 9.2 What Gets Logged
| Action | target_type | metadata |
|---|---|---|
| Block / Unblock user | user | `{ reason, previous_status }` |
| Manually verify email | user | `{}` |
| GDPR delete user | user | `{ anonymized_email }` |
| Revoke / Reinstate certificate | certificate | `{ reason, cert_id }` |
| Abort exam session | session | `{ reason }` |
| Flag session as suspicious | session | `{}` |
| Review / Escalate / Dismiss flag | question | `{ question_id, note }` |
| Add to blocklist | question | `{ stem_hash, reason }` |
| Add / Edit / Delete buffer question | question | `{ question_id, diff }` |

