## 10. Non-Functional Requirements

### 10.1 Security
- All `/api/admin/*` routes require valid JWT with `role = 'admin'`. Double-checked by `requireAdmin` middleware — no exceptions.
- Admin session shares the same 24h JWT lifespan. No "remember me" for admin.
- All admin write actions (block, revoke, delete) require the action to include a valid CSRF token (double-submit cookie pattern).
- Rate limit on admin API: 100 requests/minute per admin IP (separate bucket from user API).
- The `/admin*` frontend routes are excluded from the public sitemap and `robots.txt` (`Disallow: /admin`).
- Admin panel routes are not linked from any public page.

### 10.2 Performance
- All admin list endpoints respond within **500ms** for up to 100,000 records (requires indexes on all filter columns).
- Charts/stats endpoints respond within **1 second** (use materialized views or daily-aggregated stats table for timeseries).
- The buffer pool import endpoint accepts up to **500 questions** in a single batch.

### 10.3 Required Database Indexes
```sql
-- For user search
CREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);
CREATE INDEX idx_users_created_at ON users(created_at);
CREATE INDEX idx_users_blocked ON users(blocked);

-- For sessions filtering
CREATE INDEX idx_exam_sessions_status ON exam_sessions(status);
CREATE INDEX idx_exam_sessions_user_id ON exam_sessions(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_exam_sessions_created_at ON exam_sessions(created_at);
CREATE INDEX idx_exam_sessions_suspicious ON exam_sessions(suspicious);

-- For certificates search
CREATE INDEX idx_certificates_certificate_id ON certificates(certificate_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_certificates_user_id ON certificates(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_certificates_awarded_on ON certificates(awarded_on);
CREATE INDEX idx_certificates_revoked ON certificates(revoked);

-- For flags
CREATE INDEX idx_question_flags_status ON question_flags(status);
CREATE INDEX idx_question_flags_question_id ON question_flags(question_id);

-- For buffer pool
CREATE INDEX idx_questions_buffer ON exam_sessions(id) WHERE is_buffer = true;
```

### 10.4 Responsive Behavior
- The admin panel is **desktop-first** (min-width 1280px target).
- It is **not required to be fully mobile-responsive** — admin actions are operational tasks performed on workstations.
- A basic mobile warning banner is shown on viewports < 768px: "Admin panel is optimized for desktop browsers."

